"""PR #218 findings 3 and 10: no default selects the registry split or split v1, and the v1-port lineage check (a v1
sampler fit over every universe row, i.e. every row's target) runs only on the explicit registry replay.

  RawDefaults       tools/v2_rowsel_raw.py and its coverage route default to rowsel-raw-split-v2; v1 only explicitly;
                    the explicit v1 and v2 paths build the bytes the custody version 28be7f98 built
  BuilderDefaults   tools/v2_rowsel_build.py refuses to run without --split-version; 'registry' only when passed
  PortCheck         load_dataset refuses v1_port_check=None; only True runs sampler_select over all universe positions
                    (must-fail spy); the registry replay's lineage equals fcfe3828's
  V2Path            build_v2 (v2 and v2g) never fits the sampler over all universe positions (spy)
  BeforeAfter       a v2 and a v2g build before (custody fcfe3828) and after the change: view ids, context_sha256,
                    files, cut and every gate unchanged; only port_reproduces_v1_selection / port_fit_cpu_s differ
                    (plus the reason key added next to them)
"""
